daemon: finish a detach that hits the startup handshake

ar8030d never re-attached to its SDIO device when the device failed
while the daemon was still handshaking with it -- e.g. ar8030d started
while the chip re-enumerated from ROM to its RTOS firmware, or a write
that got EIO right after a start. Every client then got "no device"
until the daemon was restarted.

The detach (sdiorpc_8030_poll -> stop_sdio -> dev_node_force_exit ->
del_worknod) waits for every work node to be closed by dev_send_thread.
Until the device answers the handshake, the hardware node stays
writable and makes another keep-alive packet every time, and
dev_send_thread's inner loop only stops on a freed node or an empty
packet, not on a failed send: it kept sending keep-alives into the dead
device. And get_working_node() asks the hardware list first, so even
back in the outer loop the hardware node always won over the closed
callback node. del_worknod() waited forever -- in the main thread,
which is the one that polls for the device again.

Leave the inner loop when dev_send() fails (every transport returns < 0
on an error and >= 0 on success), and hand out closed work nodes before
writable ones, so a detach always finishes and the device is probed
again a second later.

Reproduced on a BetaFPV P1 air unit by starting ar8030d without waiting
for the chip's RTOS: before, "sdio detach" and nothing more, still no
device 40 s later; after, "stop subdev", "stop dev_node_list", a new
"sdio probe" one second later, the handshake, and the link came up.

diff --git a/daemon/usb_event_list.c b/daemon/usb_event_list.c
--- a/daemon/usb_event_list.c
+++ b/daemon/usb_event_list.c
@@ -94,6 +94,11 @@
     return pnod->pact->dev_write_able(pnod);
 }
 
+static int find_freed(basenode* pnod, void* par)
+{
+    return pnod && pnod->freeflag;
+}
+
 struct basenode* plist_find_work_node(dev_node_list* plist, finder fd, void* fdpar)
 {
     if (!plist || !fd) {
@@ -125,7 +130,13 @@
 static basenode* get_working_node(dev_node_list* plist)
 {
     while (plist->running & run_dev) {
-        basenode* ret = plist_find_usb_node(plist, find_work_and_del, NULL);
+        /* Work nodes being closed first: del_worknod() waits for them, and
+         * the hardware node stays writable for as long as the device never
+         * answered its keep-alive, so it would otherwise always win. */
+        basenode* ret = plist_find_work_node(plist, find_freed, NULL);
+        if (!ret) {
+            ret = plist_find_usb_node(plist, find_work_and_del, NULL);
+        }
         if (!ret) {
             ret = plist_find_work_node(plist, find_work_and_del, NULL);
         }
@@ -192,9 +203,12 @@
 
             int sdlen = tmpnod->pact->dev_pack_make(tmpnod, sndbuff, SD_BUF_LEN);
 
-            if (sdlen > 0) {
-                plist->dev_send(plist->devhandle, sndbuff, sdlen, 0);
-            } else {
+            if (sdlen <= 0) {
+                break;
+            }
+            if (plist->dev_send(plist->devhandle, sndbuff, sdlen, 0) < 0) {
+                /* The device failed: back to get_working_node(), which
+                 * hands out the nodes a detach is waiting for. */
                 break;
             }
         }
